#!/usr/bin/env python3
# ntsc-tvh - Analog NTSC tuning/streaming/scanning helper for TVHeadend pipe:// muxes
#
# Replaces the old ivtv-utils approach with v4l2-ctl + ffmpeg.
# Designed and tested against the Hauppauge WinTV-HVR-1950 (pvrusb2 driver,
# on-board hardware MPEG-2 encoder) but auto-detects raw-frame devices too.
#
# Subcommands:
#   doctor                 Check device, driver, codecs, permissions
#   list                   List channels (all, or --active-only)
#   tune    CHANNEL        Tune only (debug)
#   signal  CHANNEL        Tune + report signal strength / AFC (debug)
#   stream  CHANNEL        Tune + emit an MPEG-TS stream on stdout  <-- TVHeadend calls this
#   scan                   Scan tuner channels, save the active ones
#   m3u                    Write an M3U playlist of active channels (for TVHeadend auto-network)
#   install-timer          Install/remove a systemd timer for periodic rescan (24h or none)
#   status                 Show last-scan summary
#
# Channel IDs:   TABLE:CHANNEL          e.g.  us-bcast:7   us-cable:23   us-cable-irc:5
#                input:NAME             e.g.  input:composite   input:svideo
#
# Config precedence (low -> high): built-in defaults < /etc/ntsc-tvh.conf < environment.
# Config file is simple KEY=VALUE lines.

